\caption{Probit and grid checks of the budget law, non-linear models on German Credit ($40$ instances) and ACS Employment ($60$). (a--c) Share of correct runs against $x=g\sqrt m/\sigma$ for antithetic permutation, the \texttt{shap} Kernel explainer and the paired Kernel estimator ($m_{\mathrm{eff}}\ge256$, $R=100$ runs per point, bins of $3$--$110$ points), against $\Phi(x)$. (d) Probit slope $\beta$ (predicted $1$) by estimator and budget range, with instance-bootstrap interval. (e) Interval-censored slope of $\log m^*$ on $\log g$ under thinning of the budget grid (predicted $-2$).}
